sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS R1-R4, single-swamp-node, Recall recipe-rollout-is-automatic. docs/reference/node-provisioning.md#converge-a-node-to-a-recipe.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · recipe rollout after a release
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  Note over GW: Admit recipe for Node 12<br/>recipe sha256:… · task #5161
  %%> When:
  %%> - a deployed release carries a new machine software recipe; the Gateway visits the rollout set one Node at a time, in its window
  %%> - an operator runs `php artisan node:converge-recipe 12` on the Gateway
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - no `orbit` command; no per-five-minute Swamp poll admits it
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - Node 12 is an active managed Ubuntu Node on x86_64
  %%> - no other recipe or fleet rollout change runs on Node 12; the Gateway holds one lock per Node
  %%> - every role prerequisite is in the recipe, and no managed Tool constraint conflicts with it
  %%> What it decides:
  %%> - the desired pins: the union of Node 12's active role profiles; a roleless Node uses `operator`
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5161 recorded; the attempt is `unverified`; the last verified recipe stays recorded
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-fleet-recipe
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the pins: Ubuntu snapshot, packages, artifacts with URLs and SHA-256, PHP set, JavaScript runtimes, browser
  %%> - Node 12's address, SSH host keys and enrolled account; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  SW->>N: Inspect the Node<br/>packages · origins · PHP plan
  %%> How:
  %%> - Swamp reaches Node 12 over SSH from 209, with `@swamp/ssh`
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads installed packages and their origins, and asks `php.install-build` for its plan
  %%> Refuses:
  %%> - Docker CE (`node.recipe_docker_provider`), another PHP apt source or extra PHP packages (`node.recipe_php_refused`); then nothing changes
  SW->>N: Install pinned packages<br/>apt snapshot · no removals
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - installs missing or older Ubuntu packages and the exact artifacts, with package removal disabled, then `apt-get check`
  %%> - refreshes the snapshot indexes only when something needs installation
  %%> Busy apt lock:
  %%> - it waits for the lock within the run's time budget, then fails
  SW->>N: Install the PHP build<br/>php.install-build
  %%> When:
  %%> - only on Nodes whose roles run PHP: `app-dev`, `app-prod`, `websocket`, `gateway`
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - installs the pinned Sury build from Orbit's mirror, checks each FPM master, and puts the previous build back if a check fails
  SW->>N: Install JS runtimes<br/>Node · Vite+ · pnpm · Bun
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - installs the pinned runtimes from verified archives, without a downloaded installer
  %%> - removes a duplicate `nodejs` apt package only after the recipe runtime passes its check
  opt role app-prod
    SW->>N: Install the browser<br/>headless shell · AppArmor
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - installs the digest-pinned Chrome headless shell, root-owned, and loads its one AppArmor `userns` exception
    %%> If it fails:
    %%> - the previous AppArmor policy is put back
  end
  SW->>N: Restart changed services<br/>only changed packages
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - restarts only services of packages whose version changed; nothing else is touched
  %%> Why a restart:
  %%> - a new package version only runs after a restart; a reload keeps the old binary
  SW->>N: Check the recipe<br/>versions · service health
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks every pinned version and the health of each affected service
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the recipe only counts as applied when Node 12 shows it
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - the CLI and the Node agent; `fleet.rollout` checks those
  alt every check passes
    N-->>SW: pins installed · healthy
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the installed versions, and packages newer than the recipe
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the recipe<br/>Node 12 verified · task done
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Node 12's verified recipe becomes this version; the attempt succeeds
    %%> - task #5161 succeeds, and the Gateway admits the next Node
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: refused or exit ≠ 0
    %%> When:
    %%> - a refusal at inspection, a package, PHP, runtime or browser step fails, or a check fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Mark the attempt failed<br/>halt · rerun after a fix
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the attempt is marked failed; the last verified recipe stays recorded; task #5161 fails
    %%> - the recipe rollout halts, so later Nodes stay untouched, and an alert is raised
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - packages installed before the failure stay; a failed PHP build is replaced by the previous one
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - safe: every step skips what is already at its pin; it is a new task
  end
